|~ What is declared under `::quote`: the refusals of its
   constructor, the refusal of text read as code, and the verbs of
   quotes. A quote is also the vector of its steps, so the verbs of
   vectors read it as one, and a quote under a tag, a link or a snippet
   of a page, reads them through its shape. ~|

:quote/construct
  |~~ The quote of a vector whose every element is a step. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:quote/PayloadNotVecError
  |~~ `::quote` builds code from the vector of its steps; a payload of
      another kind is refused.
      ::link~(::quote | doc)

      ~(
        ::quote{:not :steps}
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::quote/PayloadNotVecError ::map]
       )
  ~~|

:quote/ElementNotStepError
  |~~ Every element of a quote is a step: a literal, a quote, a
      vector, a set or a map of steps, or a step as data, `::call`,
      `::proj` and their kin. A value with no reading as code, a value
      under a tag of another kind among them, is refused at the index it
      stands at.
      ::link~(::quote | doc)

      ~(
        [::Box[1]] | tag ::quote
        !| [type /index]
        |  eq [::quote/ElementNotStepError 0]
       )
  ~~|

:quote/ParseError
  |~~ The source does not read as qlang: `:marker` points where the
      reading stopped, `:expected` lists what could stand there, and a
      source cut short names the bracket it left open.
      ::link~(::quote | doc)

      ~(
        "42 |" | parse
        !| type
        |  eq ::quote/ParseError
       )
  ~~|

:quote/ParseError/source
  |~~ The line of the text where the reading stopped. ~~|
  ::string

:quote/ParseError/marker
  |~~ A caret under the place it stopped. ~~|
  ::string

:quote/ParseError/message
  |~~ What the grammar says of the place, a bracket left open among it. ~~|
  ::string

:quote/ParseError/expected
  |~~ What the reading could take there. ~~|
  ::vec

:quote/ParseError/found
  |~~ What it found there. ~~|
  ::string

:quote/ParseError/location
  |~~ The place, its offsets, lines and columns. ~~|
  ::map

:quote/ParseError/uri
  |~~ The source the text came from. ~~|
  ::string

:quote/parse
  |~~ The source text of the quote, the reverse of `parse` on a string.

      ~(~(add 1) | parse | eq "add 1")
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:quote/parse/text
  |~~ The text the quote reads back from. ~~|
  ::string

:quote/open
  |~~ The answer of the query the quote holds, run as it stands in the
      scope of the reader, beneath whatever tags stand over it: a link
      opens to the page it names, so `links * open` reads every page a
      page names in one query, and a snippet to the answer it shows.

      ~(|~~ ::link~(1 | add 1) ~~| | links | first | open | eq 2)
      ~(::qlang | doc | links * open | every ~(type | eq ::doc))
      ~(|~~ ::snippet~([3 1 2] | sort) ~~| | snippets | first | open | eq [1 2 3])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}
